coder › Done. Changes on branch `work/main`, committed as two commits:

- `8356aa5` Add `redact()` for secret fields and Bearer tokens
- `d28ef70` Redact logger fields before writing the line

## What changed

**`src/redact.ts`** (new)
- Exports `redact(value: unknown): unknown`.
- Deep-copies plain objects (including null-prototype objects) and arrays.
- For every key whose lowercased name contains `password`, `passwd`, `secret`, `token`, `apikey`, `api_key`, `api-key`, or `authorization`, replaces the value with `'[redacted]'`.
- For every string value, replaces `Bearer <token>` with `Bearer [redacted]`.
- Never mutates the input; non-plain objects and primitives pass through unchanged.

**`src/logger.ts`**
- `log()` now passes `fields` through `redact()` before spreading them into the JSON line. `level` and `message` are not redacted.

**`src/redact.test.ts`** (new)
- Covers key redaction at depth, case-insensitivity, all `api` key spellings, Bearer tokens (including multiple per string), top-level arrays/strings, unchanged values, and non-mutation.

**`src/logger.test.ts`**
- Added tests for redacted flat fields, nested fields, and Bearer tokens in fields; kept the existing one-JSON-line test.

## Checks

```
