No typecheck or lint scripts exist in `package.json` (`"test": "bun test"` is the only script), so that is the only check run.

## Decisions the plan didn't specify

- "Objects" is treated as plain objects (prototype `Object.prototype` or `null`) plus arrays. Dates, Maps, and class instances are returned as-is rather than being rebuilt, so "nothing else changes" holds and no constructor assumptions are made.
- Key matching is substring-based, exactly as "contains" says (e.g. `tokenCount` would match `token`).
- The Bearer match is case-sensitive and single-space, following the literal `'Bearer '` in the request (the "in any case" wording was applied only to key names).

